  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Premier Promoting Innovative and Resilient Agriculture Market Systems Activity</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="PT">Premier Promovendo Atividades de Sistemas de Mercado Agr&#xed;cola Inovadores e Resilientes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Mozambique):  .The Feed The Future Mozambique Promoting.Innovative and Resilient Agriculture Market Systems activity (FTF-Premier) is a.five-year investment to create sustainable change in agricultural markets and.food systems in Mozambique. FTF-Premier will focus on increased incomes,.employment, and resilience in the agriculture sector, where 80% of Mozambicans.earn their living. The activity will provide technical and financial support to.producers, agribusinesses, and other actors who participate in or support.agricultural value chains. The investments made under FTF-Premier will increase.value chain competitiveness by building on previously made development gains.and will leverage the investments of USAID and other donors to increase.adoption of improved technologies, reduce post-harvest losses, and strengthen.business organization. With FY 2022 funds, FTF-Premier will work with local.market actors, increasing the resiliency of the agricultural market system in.the Nacala Corridor to absorb, adapt, and respond to external climate,.economic, and political shocks. Improving market system-level resilience.entails not only strengthening the resilience of actors within the market.system, but also ensuring that the system itself is resilient and can continue.to provide a market for and source of goods, services and employment during and.after periods of shock. FTF-Premier will: a) exploit attractive market.opportunities where the Nacala Corridor has a comparative advantage, b).catalyze and expand local agro-processing industries, and c) work with and.through local third-party service providers as delivery partners. FTF-Premier will.also utilize a $6.4M co-investment facility to de-risk investments by.agribusiness clients and local service providers to promote catalytic business.innovations... ...</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="PT">(Mo&#xe7;ambique): A actividade Alimentar o Futuro Mo&#xe7;ambique Promovendo Sistemas de Mercado Agr&#xed;cola Inovadores e Resilientes (FTF-Premier) &#xe9; um investimento de cinco anos para criar mudan&#xe7;as sustent&#xe1;veis &#x200b;&#x200b;nos mercados agr&#xed;colas e nos sistemas alimentares em Mo&#xe7;ambique. A FTF-Premier centrar-se-&#xe1; no aumento dos rendimentos, do emprego e da resili&#xea;ncia no sector agr&#xed;cola, onde 80% dos mo&#xe7;ambicanos ganham a vida. A atividade fornecer&#xe1; apoio t&#xe9;cnico e financeiro a produtores, agroneg&#xf3;cios e outros atores que participam ou apoiam cadeias de valor agr&#xed;colas. Os investimentos feitos no &#xe2;mbito do FTF-Premier aumentar&#xe3;o a competitividade da cadeia de valor, aproveitando os ganhos de desenvolvimento anteriormente obtidos, e alavancar&#xe3;o os investimentos da USAID e de outros doadores para aumentar a adop&#xe7;&#xe3;o de tecnologias melhoradas, reduzir as perdas p&#xf3;s-colheita e fortalecer a organiza&#xe7;&#xe3;o empresarial. Com os fundos do exerc&#xed;cio financeiro de 2022, a FTF-Premier trabalhar&#xe1; com os intervenientes do mercado local, aumentando a resili&#xea;ncia do sistema de mercado agr&#xed;cola no Corredor de Nacala para absorver, adaptar-se e responder aos choques clim&#xe1;ticos, econ&#xf3;micos e pol&#xed;ticos externos. Melhorar a resili&#xea;ncia ao n&#xed;vel do sistema de mercado implica n&#xe3;o s&#xf3; refor&#xe7;ar a resili&#xea;ncia dos intervenientes no sistema de mercado, mas tamb&#xe9;m garantir que o pr&#xf3;prio sistema seja resiliente e possa continuar a fornecer um mercado e uma fonte de bens, servi&#xe7;os e emprego durante e ap&#xf3;s per&#xed;odos de choque. A FTF-Premier ir&#xe1;: a) explorar oportunidades de mercado atractivas onde o Corredor de Nacala tem uma vantagem comparativa, b).catalisar e expandir as ind&#xfa;strias locais de processamento agr&#xed;cola, ec) trabalhar com e.atrav&#xe9;s de prestadores de servi&#xe7;os terceirizados locais como parceiros de entrega. A FTF-Premier tamb&#xe9;m utilizar&#xe1; um mecanismo de co-investimento de US$ 6,4 milh&#xf5;es para reduzir o risco de investimentos de clientes do agroneg&#xf3;cio e prestadores de servi&#xe7;os locais para promover inova&#xe7;&#xf5;es empresariais catal&#xed;ticas... ...</narrative>
  </description>
